rota lap 4145, row 0 -- Aether, Jupiter, why the work exists, the row that hears. Threshold, Follow Our Compass, the Lindy Effect, the Grain and the Crossing. The row listens for the silence where a claim used to be and a witness now stands, and the grain's own fusion strand says it flatly -- a guard that cannot red guards nothing. That sentence chose the whole lap: four instruments read mantra/src/store.rye every pass and none of them could red on bytes that do not compile.
think The round opened dirty. fleet_round_open stashed a dead lap's leavings, and stash_record_scan listed 16 files standing in a stash and on no ref -- three of them a declaration-walk witness written 20260906.060019 by a lap that died before its commit. None of the three is on disk and none is in git history, so they were lost rather than landed by another route.
think The cold scoped roster refused first: an abandoned pass held the lock with its parent gone. Killed with SIGTERM as the runner's own refusal prescribes, which runs its EXIT trap and releases the lock; the retry ran 1,406s and answered guards_red=2.
think One red was index_row_bound -- today's shelf carried 20260907.023053 twice and out of order, a rebase re-applying a row whose twin already stood. Repaired first, reds before new work.
think The other red was standing_equipment reading its own roster's red, so the two are one.
think The lost witness expected mantra/src/store.rye to compile. It does not: std.mem.trimRight is retired to trimEnd in the vendored std, and read_head returns allocator.dupe without its try in a function returning an optional error union. The elder lap had found and fixed both; the fix went down with the lap.
think Then the sharper question -- how a broken file passed the census that exists to find unbuilt code. rye_compile_reach_scan classes a runner as compiling when its TEXT matches a compile spelling anywhere, then credits every .rye literal that runner names as a build root. mantra_glow_tend_limb4_witness.rish builds a Glow desk at line 44 through RYE_ZIG= and greps store.rye at lines 35 and 39 for struct fields. The grep is laundered into a build, and the census reads asserted=0.
obs Measured the exposure rather than asserting it: of 1,528 credited roots, 130 tracked .rye files are named inside a compiling runner and never on a line carrying a compile spelling. That is an UPPER bound rather than the laundered class -- comlink_recall_two_way_sync_wire_lab.rish builds through a helper, build_guest "comlink/guest_2way_fetcher_rx.rye", which a line-level reading also calls a grep. Deciding the class wants a per-site read the census does not do, so the row books the bound and names the remainder.
obs The recovered control failed on its first run for exactly the fault plant.sh was written for: its elder-ArrayList sed still named std.ArrayListUnmanaged(u32) after that type became LineId, so the phase built the unmutated module and read exit 0. Adopting plant_apply turned that into plant_matched_nothing:elder_arraylist. First adoption outside the helper's own lane.
obs Its two floor phases had the same shape in numbers: they planted 19 and 20 against a room that has grown to 31, so both passed and neither proved anything. They now read the count from the clean run's own output, so the two sides of the bound move with the room.
